• LimitedUserRole – A more restricted role, which you'll grant limited access to as the master
user.
For instructions to create the roles, see Creating a role using custom trust policies in the IAM User
Guide.
Both roles must have the following trust policy, which allows your Cognito identity pool to assume
the roles:
JSON
{
"Version":"2012-10-17",
"Statement": [{
"Effect": "Allow",
"Principal": {
"Federated": "cognito-identity.amazonaws.com"
},
"Action": "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
"Condition": {
"StringEquals": {
"cognito-identity.amazonaws.com:aud": "{identity-pool-id}"
},
"ForAnyValue:StringLike": {
"cognito-identity.amazonaws.com:amr": "authenticated"
}
}
}]
}
Note
Replace identity-pool-id with the unique identiﬁer of your Amazon Cognito identity
pool. For example, us-east-1:0c6cdba7-3c3c-443b-a958-fb9feb207aa6.
